{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLElision\/smufl","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"smufl","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSmuflLyricsGlyphName","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL23MXLSmuflLyricsGlyphNameV","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSmuflLyricsGlyphName"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"smufl"},{"text":" attribute.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"smufl","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSmuflLyricsGlyphName","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL23MXLSmuflLyricsGlyphNameV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLElisionV5smuflAA23MXLSmuflLyricsGlyphNameVSgvp","title":"smufl"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLElision"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlelision\/smufl"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The SMuFL canonical glyph name used to specify the elision symbol when the text content is empty."}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLElision":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLElision","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLElision"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlelision","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLElision"}],"title":"MXLElision","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The elision type represents an elision between lyric syllables. The text content specifies the symbol used to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"display the elision. Common values are a no-break space (Unicode 00A0), an underscore (Unicode 005F), or an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"undertie (Unicode 203F). If the text content is empty, the smufl attribute is used to specify the symbol to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"use. Its value is a SMuFL canonical glyph name that starts with lyrics. The SMuFL attribute is ignored if the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elision glyph is already specified by the text content. If neither text content nor a smufl attribute are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"present, the elision glyph is application-specific."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLElision/smufl":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLElision\/smufl","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"smufl","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL23MXLSmuflLyricsGlyphNameV","text":"MXLSmuflLyricsGlyphName","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The SMuFL canonical glyph name used to specify the elision symbol when the text content is empty."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlelision\/smufl","kind":"symbol","title":"smufl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSmuflLyricsGlyphName":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLSmuflLyricsGlyphName","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSmuflLyricsGlyphName","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The smufl-lyrics-glyph-name type is used to reference a specific Standard Music Font Layout (SMuFL) lyrics"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elision character. The value is a SMuFL canonical glyph name that starts with lyrics."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSmuflLyricsGlyphName","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLSmuflLyricsGlyphName","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsmufllyricsglyphname"}}}